    {
      "id": "15382101-073e-42a1-86dc-418a0f789cf2",
      "title": "Dangerous Goods",
      "lessons": [
        {
          "id": "7c72e9fe-dbb9-4f04-8d1b-df8a3448ed7a",
          "title": "Definition of DG",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "id": "1596a7ec-473d-471a-8651-ff951050fe22",
              "type": "text",
              "content": {
                "html": "<h3 style=\"text-align: center;\"> Understanding Dangerous Goods</h3><p></p>"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "1bddf301-062c-46c0-b498-bedea9bd5bc4",
              "type": "accordion",
              "content": {
                "items": [
                  {
                    "id": "7d6b6420-43a3-4756-b676-365a29372358",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "id": "985c9448-e167-4203-abe2-e43e11ca5523",
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "<p>Articles or substances which are capable of posing a risk to health, safety, property or the environment and which are shown in the list of dangerous goods in the Technical Instructions or which are classified according to those Instructions.</p>"
                      }
                    ],
                    "title": "What are Dangerous Goods (DG)?"
                  },
                  {
                    "id": "3d6612db-43a8-4262-b0cb-ef81d65b18fa",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "id": "0c44fdce-8a96-4482-bfcd-3f4cf27c9df5",
                        "type": "text",
                        "content": "<p>Dangerous Goods are things that can cause harm to people, property, or the environment. They are listed or grouped in official safety instructions.</p>"
                      }
                    ],
                    "title": "Simplified Definition"
                  }
                ],
                "allowMultiple": false
              }
            }
          ]
        },
